error[L0363]: macro code ran too many steps
  --> expand/macro_steps_charge_a_closure_chain.knv:13:42
   |
13 |                   (defn main () (println (chains 2000))))
   |                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this call passed 35000 macro steps
   |
   = note: the macro calls in one top-level form run at most 35000 steps: a function call or a `recur` costs one step per expression of the body it runs, an `expand-call` costs 64 and one per form it returns, a closure costs one step and one per binding in scope, and a built-in costs one step per list item it copies or reads and one for every 16 bytes of text it reads, and `closest-name` one step for each pair of bytes it compares between the name and the candidates
   = help: make the macro stop, or wrap the top-level form in `(with-macro-steps 30000000 ...)`
